  "body": "### Summary\n\nAs a user long-pressing a favourite, I want the context menu to list only what I can do now, as the HIG asks for context menus, so that the menu is not padded with dimmed entries.\n\n### Rule\n\n\"Hide unavailable menu items, don't dim them. Unlike a regular menu, which helps people discover actions they can perform even when the action isn't available, a context menu displays only the actions that are relevant to the currently selected view or content.\" — [HIG › Context menus](https://developer.apple.com/design/human-interface-guidelines/context-menus) (Best practices; page updated 2023-12-05).\n\n### What the app does (dev-swift @ `7a61018f`)\n\n`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicListView.swift`:\n- `:244-247`: « Filtrer les posts » with `.disabled(filtering.isBusy)`;\n- `:241` with `:198-206`: `removeButton` in the menu, « Suppression… » with `.disabled(removing)`.\n\n### Legacy at `87fe0d1c`\n\nSame: `.disabled(isRemoving)` at `HFRswift/Swift/MainWindow.swift:656`, `.disabled(isRemovingFavorite)` at `Favorites.swift:1166`.\n\n### Class\n\n**(b) evolution, M5** (same as legacy, not an accessibility matter).\n\n### Proposed fix and check\n\n- Leave the entry out of the `contextMenu` builder while it cannot run (`if !filtering.isBusy { … }`, `if !removing { … }`); keep the disabled state on the swipe button only.\n- Check: a view-model test of the entries built while busy.\n\nRelated: #897 (context menus, another aspect).\n\nFound by #866 (cloud/r866-fable, Fable 5.2)",
